## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates robust multi-hand 3D pose with fine-grained articulation under occlusion, plus on-device adaptation for real-world diversity.

## Key Concepts
- 3D hand pose (finger joints), hand mesh (MANO)
- Temporal tracking and occlusion handling
- On-device few-shot adaptation and edge latency

## Code Example
```javascript
function totalLoss(key3d, pred3d, mesh3d, predMesh3d, tio, contactPred, contactGT){
  const lKey = mse(key3d, pred3d);
  const lMesh = l2(mesh3d, predMesh3d);
  const lTemp = mse(pred3d, tio);
  const lContact = crossEntropy(contactGT, contactPred);
  return 0.4*lKey + 0.3*lMesh + 0.2*lTemp + 0.1*lContact;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate hand-object contact reliability in clutter?
- What ablations would you run to isolate the impact of articulation accuracy vs. contact estimation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge deployment, privacy-preserving CV, multi-camera fusion, and rapid adaptation to new attire in a security context.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference, privacy-preserving anonymization, cross-camera re-ID, multi-camera tracking, 5-shot adaptation, latency.
- Synthetic+real data, losses for detection, embedding, privacy, and association.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch for a privacy-preserving forward pass
function forward(frame, model) {
  const det = model.detect(frame);
  const emb = model.embed(det.boxes);
  const blurred = blurFaces(frame, det.faces);
  return { blurred, det, emb };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce privacy guarantees across jurisdictions?
- How would you measure cross-camera re-ID stability over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests designing a monocular system that operates in a dynamic warehouse, combining SLAM with object pose estimation, plus on-device few-shot adaptation under tight latency.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular SLAM with dynamic object handling
- 6-DoF pose estimation for rigid objects
- On-device 5-shot adaptation (meta-learning prototypes)
- Synthetic+real data with domain randomization
- Efficient losses: reprojection, pose consistency, temporal coherence

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for data association and pose update
function updatePose(frame, map, adptModel) {
  const detections = adptModel.detect(frame);
  const associations = associate(detections, map);
  map.updateWithObservations(associations);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify long-term map drift versus dynamic object tracking reliability?
- How would you extend to multi-camera fusion on a drone swarm?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical CV pipeline using lightweight, non-ML methods for a common task.

## Key Concepts
- Circle detection with Hough transform
- Radius-based grouping for coin types
- Noise/shadow handling with blur and histogram equalization
- Validation with synthetic data

## Code Example
```javascript
// OpenCV.js-like pseudocode
let src = cv.imread('table.jpg');
cv.cvtColor(src, src, cv.COLOR_RGBA2GRAY);
cv.equalizeHist(src, src);
cv.GaussianBlur(src, new cv.Size(9,9), 2);
let circles = new cv.Mat();
cv.HoughCircles(src, circles, cv.HOUGH_GRADIENT, 1.2, 20, 50, 30, 10, 60);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you address perspective distortions?
- How would you validate robustness with lighting changes?
